// Files (M6 Task 10).
//
// `read_file(path)` and `write_file(path, body)` are builtins, not functions in
// this module: the names live in the one shared scope, so a wrapper would be a
// duplicate definition. They are documented here because this is the module a
// reader looks in for them.
//
// `read_file` answers `Result[string, io.Error]`: the whole file as a fresh
// owned string, or the error that stopped it. A missing file and an empty file
// are different answers. `write_file` answers `Result[void, io.Error]` -- `1`/`0`
// was a boolean pretending to be an error. Match the `Result`, or propagate it
// with `?` from a function that returns one.
//
// The current directory is `getcwd()`, which answers the same `Result`; it is
// documented in `os.ya` beside the process builtins.
//
// Ownership: neither consumes its argument; both results are owned.
